"""Mathematical rule premises and operational recipe defects."""
import hashlib,json,pathlib,runpy
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_operad_skills_remaining';runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_synthesis12.py')));fs=json.loads((H/(P+'_preparation.json')).read_text())['files'];p=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())
def e(i,a,b):return {'path':fs[i]['path'],'sha256':fs[i]['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
def f(n,t,b,ev,a,v,severity='medium'):return {'id':f'OPSKILL-F{n:03}','severity':severity,'title':t,'finding':b,'evidence':ev,'recommended_action':a,'validation':v}
rows=[
f(107,'Strict Boolean recipe rejects every Boolean','isinstance(v,bool) and not isinstance(v,(int,str)) rejects True and False since bool subclasses int. This normative recipe cannot admit any valid Boolean record.',[e(495,31,37)],'Use type(v) is bool or isinstance(v,bool) and test both valid Booleans plus integers/strings; use explicit exceptions rather than assert for production.','CHECK-087 evaluates all relevant finite examples.','high'),
f(108,'Skill root path recipe has an off-by-one parent index','The stated .agents/skills/name/scripts/file.py hierarchy has repository root at file.parents[4]; parents[3] is .agents. The os.path dirname plus four ascents alternative is correct, so the supposedly equivalent recipes disagree.',[e(490,11,14)],'Use script-relative verified root resolution and test the actual installed hierarchy; do not mix dirname ascent count with Path.parents index.','CHECK-088 gives exact paths.'),
f(109,'Cochain dimension and coordinate bounds need explicit representative restrictions','For a3-cycle without2-faces every standard edge is closed and has quotient l1 distance1. These raw surviving cochains span dimension3, but beta1=1; equality applies to quotient classes or chosen complementary representatives. Positive observer weights and quotient descent likewise do not bound arbitrary raw gauge coordinates: d0=[-1,1], c=cprime=100 has quotient norm0.',[e(492,19,28),e(493,11,14),e(493,26,27)],'State whether survivors are classes, harmonic/optimal residuals or raw cochains. Require norm-bounded representative and actual per-observer descent before using coordinate inequality; keep quotient and representative norms distinct.','CHECK-089 gives primal/dual witnesses and ranks; CHECK-090 gives exact coordinate counterexample.','high'),
f(110,'Trace-distance product formula omits real normalized domain','The product one-half norm(a-b) norm(a+b) computes rank-one trace distance for normalized real vectors. It fails for allowed-looking complex unit vectors a=1,b=i: both densities are[1] yet product1. Unnormalized vectors also need scale treatment.',[e(492,36,42),e(492,56,58)],'Declare real unit-sphere domain or use phase-invariant complex formula with normalization/zero checks; distinguish lift fibers from signed cochain orientation.','CHECK-091 records exact unit-phase counterexample.'),
f(111,'Dual flow statement reverses complementary slackness and closure statement is overbroad','Source says nonzero edge flow requires zero residual. In weighted l1 duality nonzero residual requires y=w*sign(r), while zero residual permits any bounded feasible dual coordinate. Source also says norms cannot determine closure; a correctly computed definite exact norm(d1r)=0 is exactly closure, although norm(r) alone cannot determine exactness and unbound scalar claims are not certificates.',[e(500,27,34),e(500,46,53)],'Correct signed saturation/free-zero-coordinate conditions and distinguish actual computed exact norm from an unverified scalar or seminorm. Preserve actual operators/certificates in receipts.','CHECK-092 exhibits primal=dual=1 with nonzero r,y; CHECK-093 states exact norm equivalence.','high'),
f(112,'Encoding repair policy identifies valid mathematical Unicode as corruption','Documentation manager lists valid Phi, lambda, arrows and middle dots as mojibake and mandates automatic repair; lint policy additionally standardizes to dollar delimiters then says to flag/replace those same delimiters. These instructions can rewrite sound mathematical source without evidence of corruption.',[e(452,47,54),e(451,73,81)],'Require byte/decoding diagnosis and explicit before/after provenance; preserve valid Unicode and state one noncontradictory supported delimiter grammar.','Full source-body comparison; no source rewritten.'),
f(113,'Rule corpus contains mutually conflicting canonical contracts','Same architecture rule forbids reexports then requires public __all__ reexports; triad manager manifests are mandated while persona manifests are permanently retired; exact rational JSON is p/q-only in one rule but unit denominators must omit slash in another. Historical and scoped exceptions need explicit precedence to avoid incompatible gates.',[e(453,35,40),e(453,60,69),e(481,47,61),e(489,15,24),e(498,28,30),e(496,54,55)],'Version and scope rules by current owner/profile; retain historical definitions as historical and make policy conflict an explicit refusal rather than automatic source mutation.','Full text comparison; related F052 policy conflicts preserved.'),
f(114,'Absent constructive instance is incorrectly equated with uninhabitability','A rule says an axiom set without an exhibited constructive inhabitant is an uninstantiable specification. Absence of an exhibited instance is absence of positive evidence, not proof that no instance exists. Requiring an instance for promotion is a defensible policy, with a different logical claim.',[e(494,38,50)],'Label instance status unestablished/unavailable, reserve inconsistent or uninhabitable for a proof, and distinguish by-construction subtype theorems from external adequacy.','Direct logical distinction; no external formal library replay.'),
f(115,'Set-plus-count exhaustion predicate assumes unique identifiers','Equal sets and equal list lengths can pass when duplicate multiplicities differ: declared[a,a,b] and checked[a,b,b]. Exact inventory/candidate binding requires unique IDs or multiset agreement, not counts and sets alone.',[e(498,41,45)],'Validate unique identifiers at ingress or compare canonical multisets while binding each checked result to candidate bytes.','CHECK-094; bounded predicate issue, not a claim current owners admit duplicate IDs.'),
f(116,'Rational squared lengths do not force every deficit to be irrational','Mathematical hygiene says rational positive squared edge lengths yield transcendental angles/deficits and delta notin Q. A flat Euclidean triangulated square fan has squared lengths1,2 and deficit0. Nonzero angle/deficit hypotheses cannot be omitted.',[e(484,21,24)],'State the precise nonzero algebraic-exponential hypotheses and allow exactly flat rational-zero deficits; retain interval exclusions only for claimed nonzero curvature.','CHECK-096 exact flat fan construction.'),
f(117,'Epsilon-set ranking differs from strict primary priority in the same rule','The global epsilon policy first admits candidates within epsilon of minimal discrete score, then selects near-minimal Xi, so it may choose a strictly worse primary score. This conflicts with the nearby strict lexicographic priority requirement even though it avoids pairwise tolerance cycles.',[e(492,36,53)],'Declare two distinct policies with explicit selection contract or apply exact lexicographic ordering; bind policy/epsilon into receipts and tests.','CHECK-095 selects B(primary1/2,Xi0) over A(primary0,Xi100) at epsilon1.')]
d={x['id']:x for x in r['findings']};d.update({x['id']:x for x in rows});r['findings']=list(d.values())
r['claims'].append({'id':'OPSKILL-C011','claim':'The rule corpus contains useful conditional mathematical and evidence boundaries: d1d0=0 gives norm(d1omega)<=operator_norm(d1)*Phi1, exact implies closed, gauge shifts preserve quotient class; trusted external chain tips distinguish complete history from an intact prefix; rules explicitly distinguish candidate/partial/enforced status.','evidence':[e(492,19,25),e(498,23,27),e(494,15,21),e(468,11,14),e(468,25,35)],'dependencies':['Finite normed real/rational cochain carrier, exact quotient minimum or infimum and bounded linear d1','Trusted independently pinned tip and correctly checked complete serialization','Actual named checker implementation and bounded negative controls for enforcement'],'limitations':['Closed does not imply exact without vanishing cohomology/additional premise','No local or global section theorem follows merely from d squared zero','Positive field/status declarations are not execution evidence or detector adequacy']})
r['claims']=list({x['id']:x for x in r['claims']}.values())
vp=H/(P+'_checks12.json');v={'path':'dag/reviews/'+vp.name,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(vp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'description':'Ten finite source-recipe/mathematical controls; no retained owner execution.'};r['validation']=[x for x in r['validation']if x['path']!=v['path']]+[v];p.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\n')
(H/(P+'.md')).write_text('\n'.join(['# Operad skills audit — in progress','',f"**{r['full_source_read_count']}/{r['scope_count']} full bodies reviewed; {len(r['remaining_work'])} pending.** Per-file source hashes/ranges and assessments are in JSON.",'',f"{len(r['claims'])} claims, {len(r['findings'])} findings;95 observed independent controls and one unavailable shell control.",'','Useful components include exact primal/dual witnesses, typed evidence boundaries, candidate/enforced rule status, external chain-tip custody and normalized textual matching. New rule controls expose impossible Boolean validation, wrong root indexing, representative-versus-quotient confusion, missing trace-distance domain assumptions, reversed complementary slackness and incompatible ranking policies.','','These are source review and bounded independent controls, not replay of retained workflows, native tests or providers. All original source bytes remain untouched.'])+'\n');print(json.dumps({'full':r['full_source_read_count'],'findings':len(r['findings'])}))
